WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.910
A sovereign card asks one question:

2
00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.200
in, or out.

3
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.640
A Rotation card asks a harder one:

4
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.660
of these five, which one?

5
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.060
Or none?

6
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.280
This is Rotation 1D today.

7
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.850
Five legs: Bitcoin, Ether,

8
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.880
Solana, Sui, and tokenized gold.

9
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.340
And a sixth option:

10
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.040
cash.

11
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.760
Today it holds none of them.

12
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.360
That is a decision too.

13
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.200
Open it.

14
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.960
The ribbon is the whole story.

15
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.800
Each color is one asset.

16
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.400
Green is cash.

17
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.480
Rotation never holds two at once:

18
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.040
it picks the strongest leg,

19
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.580
and leaves when it stops being the strongest.

20
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.980
Watch the switches, bar by bar.

21
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.000
September eleventh: Ether.

22
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.200
September nineteenth: Solana.

23
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.040
One day later: Sui.

24
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.860
Sometimes the strongest leg changes in a day.

25
00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.000
Then Sui for twenty-eight days.

26
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.810
And on October eighteenth:

27
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:51.480
cash.

28
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.060
Every move is decided at the daily close,

29
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.760
never in the middle of the day.

30
00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.000
The last trade, in plain words:

31
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Sui, bought September twentieth,

32
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.920
sold October eighteenth.

33
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.080
Plus thirteen point six percent in twenty-eight days.

34
00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.960
Simulated, not real money.

35
00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.540
And the two numbers that matter:

36
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.920
what one thousand dollars became with the rule,

37
00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.490
next to buying and holding the same coins,

38
00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.240
equal weight.

39
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.080
Same windows as every card:

40
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.760
six months, one year,

41
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.200
two years, or since the start.

42
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.200
And in the Lab,

43
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.960
the same story as one equity curve:

44
00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.200
each color is the asset it held.

45
00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.000
Gray is cash.

46
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.040
Proportional is the same engine.

47
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.720
Same five legs, same daily close.

48
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.120
The difference is what it does when

49
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.960
more than one leg is strong.

50
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.280
Here is a real day:

51
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.590
September twentieth.

52
00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.720
Winner put everything into Sui.

53
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.800
Proportional saw three strong legs and split the book:

54
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.960
Solana forty-four percent, Sui twenty-nine,

55
00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.440
Ether twenty-seven.

56
00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.740
The stronger the leg,

57
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.080
the bigger the slice.

58
00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.720
When a leg stops being strong,

59
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.440
it leaves, and the book is re-split among the ones that remain.

60
00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.160
October eighth: Ether and Solana are out,

61
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.200
and Sui holds the whole book.

62
00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.200
Ten days later: cash.

63
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.240
Why split?

64
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.730
One asset's bad day weighs less when it is a

65
00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.960
third of the book instead of all of it.

66
00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.440
That is the trade-off.

67
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.010
Winner concentrates, and moves harder,

68
00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:13.640
both ways.

69
00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.560
Proportional spreads the exposure,

70
00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.440
and tends to move more smoothly.

71
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.200
Neither is right for everyone.

72
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.740
Each card shows its own return and drawdown,

73
00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.650
simulated.

74
00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:23.760
You choose.

